From 253f484aab048f61fc44fc0e8366a01bac8b0f24 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "mujiburrahimank@maxlinear.com"
 <mujiburrahimank@lvdocker7.lvsw.maxlinear.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 20:52:40 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] WLANRTSYS-104974 BSS color changes after 5G radio toggle,
 client ping fails

Problem : After a 5GHz radio disable/enable with a connected client, the
client reconnects but ping fails because the BSS color in the beacon is
different from the one configured before the toggle.

Root Cause : A config reload received while the 5GHz interface is
disabled fails with a false HT capability error. The reload exits
before the old BSS color is restored, so a random color is used when
the interface is enabled again.

Resolution :
- Keep the old config if a reload fails, so a half-applied config is
  never used.

System Impact : Config reload with a disabled interface, HE BSS color

Validation : 5GHz radio toggle with connected client and continuous
ping; BSS color unchanged and ping continues

Fixup : WLANRTSYS-55139 HE BSS color
---
 src/ap/hostapd.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ap/hostapd.c b/src/ap/hostapd.c
index 29d5f53fe..7bc131f67 100644
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -381,6 +381,12 @@ int hostapd_reload_config(struct hostapd_iface *iface)
 	if (mxl_hostapd_prepare_reload_config(iface) < 0) {
 		wpa_printf(MSG_ERROR,
 				   "Failed to prepare config for reload");
+		/* Roll back: keep using the old config. Leaving iface->conf
+		 * pointing at newconf would make the next interface enable use
+		 * a config that never got he_op (BSS color) etc. restored from
+		 * the old one, i.e. a different random BSS color. */
+		iface->conf = oldconf;
+		hostapd_config_free(newconf);
 		return -1;
 	}
 	/* Restoring user configured cw on reload */
